# mcp/jev — jev-1.13-free (opencode-zen System One decision model) MCP server.
# Pure stdlib MCP (no pip deps).
#
# jev-1.13-free is reached ONLY at /zen/v1/systemone with the OpenCode desktop
# fingerprint (UA opencode/1.18.31 + x-opencode-client: desktop + x-opencode-project:
# global). Auth:
#   * REAL key -> Authorization: Bearer <OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY>  (preferred)
#   * NO key   -> Authorization: Bearer public  (relay free-tier, PR #1 — verified
#     HTTP 200 for jev-1.13-free). Truly anonymous (no Authorization) -> 403
#     FreeTierError. Non-free models require a real key.
# No fallback to any other model — JEV_MODEL is fixed to jev-1.13-free.
#
# The opencode-zen key is NOT set here: mcp-jev reads the dev profile's
# OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY straight from ~/.hermes/profiles/dev/.env at runtime (Hermes
# does not inject profile secrets into MCP subprocesses). Never commit it.
# optional — the server defaults these; uncomment only to override
# JEV_MODEL=jev-1.13-free
# JEV_ENDPOINT=https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/systemone
JEV_MCP=1          # on (default); set 0 to disable trimmer behaviour
JEV_DEBUG=0        # emit [jev-debug] POST/resp traces to stderr
